# Extend glossary with terms introduced by v0.3.0.
v030_glossary_rows = [
('ICMP','Internet Control Message Protocol carries network-layer diagnostics and error information.','cloud','cloud-icmp'),
('Longest-prefix match','Routing rule that selects the most specific destination prefix that matches an IP address.','cloud','cloud-routing-table'),
('IPv6','Version 6 of the Internet Protocol, using 128-bit addresses and IPv6-specific neighbor discovery.','cloud','cloud-ipv6-basics'),
('Signal','Asynchronous notification sent to a Unix-like process, such as SIGTERM or SIGKILL.','cloud','cloud-linux-processes'),
('Kerberos','Ticket-based network authentication protocol widely used by Active Directory.','cloud','cloud-kerberos'),
('Conditional Access','Policy evaluation at sign-in that can require controls such as MFA or compliant devices.','cloud','cloud-conditional-access'),
('Container','Process-isolation packaging model that typically shares the host operating-system kernel.','cloud','cloud-containers-vms'),
('3-2-1 backup','Resilience guideline using multiple copies across different storage or failure domains with one offsite or isolated copy.','cloud','cloud-backup-321'),
('Pipeline','Processor organization that overlaps instruction stages to improve throughput.','advanced','advanced-pipeline'),
('Branch prediction','CPU technique that predicts control flow so speculative execution can continue before a branch resolves.','advanced','advanced-branch-prediction'),
('TLB','Translation Lookaside Buffer, a cache of recent virtual-to-physical address translations.','advanced','advanced-tlb'),
('False sharing','Cache-coherence overhead caused when independent writable variables share one cache line.','advanced','advanced-false-sharing'),
('Roofline model','Performance model relating arithmetic intensity to compute throughput and memory bandwidth ceilings.','advanced','advanced-roofline'),
('Warp','A group of GPU threads scheduled together on NVIDIA architectures.','advanced','advanced-gpu-warp'),
('Collective operation','Group communication primitive such as broadcast, reduce, scatter, or gather.','advanced','advanced-mpi-collectives'),
('Consensus','Distributed agreement on ordered state despite communication delays and some failures.','advanced','advanced-consensus'),
('Entanglement','Quantum property of a joint state that cannot be factored into independent subsystem states.','advanced','advanced-entanglement'),
('Hash table','Data structure that maps keys to storage locations using a hash function and collision handling.','software','software-hash-table'),
('Binary search tree','Ordered tree structure where keys in left and right subtrees follow a comparison invariant.','software','software-tree'),
('Graph','Model of vertices and edges used to represent relationships and network-like structure.','software','software-graph'),
('Normalization','Relational schema design practice that reduces redundancy and update anomalies.','software','software-normalization'),
('Isolation level','Database guarantee controlling what concurrent transactions can observe about one another.','software','software-isolation'),
('Feature flag','Runtime control that separates deployment of code from exposure of a feature.','software','software-feature-flags'),
('Salt','Unique random value combined with a password before password hashing to defeat precomputed lookup attacks.','cyber','cyber-password-storage'),
('Session token','Credential representing an authenticated application session.','cyber','cyber-session'),
('XSS','Cross-Site Scripting, where untrusted content is executed as code in another user’s browser context.','cyber','cyber-xss'),
('SQL injection','Injection flaw where untrusted data changes the structure or meaning of a SQL query.','cyber','cyber-sql-injection'),
('SSRF','Server-Side Request Forgery, where an attacker causes a server to make unintended network requests.','cyber','cyber-ssrf'),
('EDR','Endpoint Detection and Response technology for endpoint telemetry, detection, investigation, and containment.','cyber','cyber-edr'),
('SIEM','Security Information and Event Management platform for centralized event search, correlation, and alerting.','cyber','cyber-siem'),
('Service owner','Accountable role for a technology service’s lifecycle, reliability, risk, and improvement.','leadership','leadership-service-owner'),
('Incident severity','Classification of an incident based on impact and response needs.','leadership','leadership-severity'),
('Capacity planning','Forecasting demand and ensuring sufficient resources and failure headroom.','leadership','leadership-capacity'),
('CapEx','Capital expenditure associated with assets or investments that provide value across accounting periods.','leadership','leadership-budget-capex-opex'),
('OpEx','Operating expenditure associated with ongoing costs of running the organization.','leadership','leadership-budget-capex-opex'),
('Vendor lock-in','Switching cost created by proprietary technology, contracts, data gravity, skills, or integrations.','leadership','leadership-vendor-lockin'),
('Limit','Value a function approaches as its input approaches a point.','math','math-limits'),
('Chain rule','Calculus rule for differentiating composed functions by multiplying nested sensitivities.','math','math-chain-rule'),
('Gradient','Vector of partial derivatives pointing toward steepest local increase.','math','math-gradient'),
('Determinant','Scalar describing volume scaling, orientation, and singularity of a square linear transformation.','math','math-determinant'),
('Orthogonality','Zero inner-product relationship generalizing perpendicularity.','math','math-orthogonality'),
('Combinatorics','Mathematics of counting discrete arrangements and selections.','math','math-combinatorics'),
('Floating point','Finite binary representation used to approximate real-valued numbers in computers.','math','math-numerical-error'),
('Dimensional analysis','Checking physical relationships using the dimensions and units of quantities.','physics','physics-dimensions'),
('Centripetal acceleration','Inward acceleration required for circular motion, with magnitude v²/r.','physics','physics-circular-motion'),
('Torque','Rotational effect of a force about an axis or pivot.','physics','physics-torque'),
('Simple harmonic motion','Oscillation produced by a restoring acceleration proportional to displacement.','physics','physics-shm'),
('Capacitance','Charge stored per unit potential difference, C=Q/V.','physics','physics-capacitance'),
('Faraday’s law','Law relating induced electromotive force to changing magnetic flux.','physics','physics-faraday'),
('de Broglie wavelength','Matter-wave relation λ=h/p connecting momentum and wavelength.','physics','physics-debroglie'),
('Uncertainty principle','Quantum lower bound on simultaneous spreads of certain pairs of observables.','physics','physics-uncertainty'),
]
glossary.extend(dict(term=t,definition=d,domain=dom,lesson_id=lid) for t,d,dom,lid in v030_glossary_rows)

